{"id":"search-index","parent":"perfc-search","ord":"a0","title":"A maintained search index — stop scanning the whole vault per query","done":"2026-08-24T21:33:02-04:00","desc":"- Today a query is a substring scan over every node and document body — O(corpus bytes) per keystroke. Folding is memoized; the scan is not.\n- The fix: an index maintained incrementally at the fold seam (an edit updates only what changed), serving the existing substring grammar (trigram or suffix-automaton class — not a tokenizer, which would change what matches).\n- Since search went server-side, server-only engines (bun:sqlite FTS5) are first-class candidates.\n- Start with a benchmark of body-scan cost at realistic vault sizes, so adoption is a number, not a feeling.\n- Brainstorm: brainstorming/search-index.md.","after":["search-server-side"],"created":"2026-08-19T16:46:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T21:33:02-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","brainstorm":"brainstorming/search-index.md","brief":"briefs/sidx.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24 19:03","from":"human 2026-08-19 (PR #258 question)","merge":"APPROVED by the human 20:14 (manual test passed) + AUTOMERGE their word 20:15 — reviews folded + CI green, then the orchestrator merges, no further ask","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/374 — MERGED 90460125","worktree":".worktrees/search-index"}}
{"id":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","parent":"perfc-model","ord":"a0","title":"The O(n) sweep: whole-corpus costs still paid per edit","desc":"- The one catalogue of every place where work grows with the WHOLE VAULT (all files, all nodes, all dated history) but is paid on every small event — a keystroke, a write, a tool call. **The human's rule (2026-08-24): a vault with 1000 files should not do O(1000) work per event unless the answer inherently needs it.** Costs that scale with something else — one page, one conversation, one message — are deliberately out of scope and were pruned from this tree (the 2026-08-24 re-audit found a chat-stream quadratic family and some page-sized browser leftovers; they live in the trash if ever wanted). Already-fixed costs aren't re-listed.\n- Two audits live here: the original 2026-08-19 tree audit, and the 2026-08-24 re-audit (four parallel Opus subagents over format, server+surface, ops+chat, web client), which re-verified the originals and folded everything into the area groups below.\n- Measured anchors (2026-08-19): filter ~9.6ms/keystroke warm at 20k nodes; composer ~10ms; deriving 51.4ms/frame at 980 files (28ms of it the framework merge, dying upstream).\n- The 2026-08-24 one-line summary: **the browser is now clean — the server took over the walking.** The vault-in-browser series killed the client-side vault walks; the corpus-scaled costs now live in the server's per-tab recomputation, in git-per-write, and in the model's date/tag/validation bookkeeping.\n- **Shape: these are standing costs, not PRs.** Each leaf is one cost with evidence and a fix shape; most are one PR-sized fix on their own. A leaf graduates to a `PR:` title when it is actually dispatched — the features.olai convention — rather than being pre-carved here.\n- Rough ranking: streams-per-tab and git-per-write dominate; the agenda/date/tag costs grow with the vault's age, which is the axis this vault actually grows on; validation is paid on every single write.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:38:12-04:00","custom":{"anchors-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: the measured anchors describe a browser that no longer exists — the 51.4ms/frame derive at 980 files was answered (kolu#2187 per model-indices.md:135; #279 deleted the whole-set fold and DerivedProvider, reading.tsx is pane-scoped) and the 9.6ms/keystroke filter predates search going server-side (#270). The sweep's remaining costs are the SERVER-side children below; the browser figures should be struck or re-measured post-flip","nightly-plan":"CONVERGED 2026-08-24 ~16:40 — the orchestrator × the sweep's author (Fable, 30f81ddc), debate on the human's instruction. NIGHT 1, parallel, both auto: A list-documents-bytes (gate: listing-sizes ≡ recompute-from-body test; bench artifact on a synthetic 5k corpus) ∥ B filter-scope (gate: a NEW reusable differential harness — old walk vs new over generated corpora + the real vault, set AND order equality, an under:-through-a-mirror scenario, an edit-then-requery invalidation test; auto iff harness green, ANY divergence parks the lane; bench artifact). NIGHT 2, sequential from night-1 master: C published-maps first (gate: delta-stream equivalence — a fake subscriber replays an op corpus against old and new, identical delta sequence + identical final readAll; the identity hazard is reused shells swallowing deltas; invalidation test; alloc bench; auto iff the harness lands, else the lane SELF-DEMOTES to held and says why), then D validate-incremental as SHADOW (property test: random op sequences, incremental verdict ≡ full verdict; full stays authoritative; divergence → loud alarm; auto — behavior unchanged by construction). THE FLIPS (validate incremental-only; published drops the old path) are one-liner PRs, merge=HUMAN, gated machine-checkably on divergence-log=empty ∧ soak≥3 quiet nights. AMENDMENTS: the soak is time-bounded — flip-or-remove within 7 days, default REMOVE the shadow wiring (the harness and property test STAY — the durable artifact); divergence alarms wire into the orchestrator's morning summary and a non-empty log auto-freezes the flip. Perf numbers are reported artifacts, never CI gates"}}
{"id":"perf-dates-index","parent":"psw2-model","ord":"a6","title":"Dates are derived at view time over every node, stored nowhere — agenda/calendar/day pay a full walk per edit anywhere","done":"2026-08-20T04:34:18-04:00","desc":"- `dates.ts:231` `datedNodes` flatMaps every record, no memo, no WeakMap; `agenda.ts:6` says it in so many words.\n- `App.tsx:99`'s agenda memo re-runs on every derivation change (= every edit in the vault).\n- `datedDays` (`dates.ts:275`) is a second independent full walk per month navigated.\n- `datedOn` → full walk per day-page resolution.\n- **The fix** shape the house already owns: a dated index on `Derived`, maintained by the patcher like `taggedBy`.","after":["search-server-side"],"created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:30:23-04:00","custom":{"pr":"#278 merged 563c6d3d"}}
{"id":"perf-validate-incremental","parent":"psw2-model","ord":"a5V","title":"Five of six validation rules walk every record #nightly","todo":true,"desc":"- Only checkTargets reads an index; the duplicate-id, parent, after-acyclicity, mirror-containment and doc checks iterate the whole set (validate.ts:105-110).\n- Every write and every publishing probe pays it.\n- The narrowing is named in model-indices.md:139 (re-run the cycle check only when edges changed) and still unbuilt.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T20:41:32-04:00","custom":{"dispatch-trigger":"overnight queue #3: dispatches when published-maps merges and an Opus slot is free — Opus, SHADOW only (behavior unchanged by construction), AUTO","pointers-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: substance unchanged, pointers drifted — the six rule calls are validate.ts:114-119; reportDuplicateIds:293, checkParents:312, checkAfterAcyclic:422, checkMirrorContainment:446, checkDocs:480 iterate derived.nodes; only checkTargets:387 reads derived.namedBy; the narrowing is model-indices.md:57"}}
{"id":"perf-published-maps","parent":"psw2-server","ord":"a4","title":"Publishing rebuilds about 3× O(files) of Maps per revision #nightly","todo":true,"desc":"- changeOf builds a fresh entries Map over every file, and is called three times per revision (outlines, documents, heads), plus a broken-map copy and the documents split (published.ts:141,155,190,228-241).\n- Unchanged entries are carried by reference (correct) — it's the Map shells that get re-minted every revision.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T20:41:32-04:00","custom":{"dispatch-trigger":"overnight queue #2 (night-2 pulled forward): dispatches when pldb AND filter-scope are merged (night-1 master) and an Opus slot is free — Opus, AUTO iff the delta-stream equivalence harness lands, else self-demotes to held","pointers-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: substance unchanged, lines drifted — changeOf is published.ts:231 (entries Map at :240), call sites :177 documents / :283 outlines / :304 heads, broken-map copy :280"}}
{"id":"perf-list-documents-bytes","parent":"psw2-ops","ord":"a4","title":"list_documents re-reads every .md just to report sizes #nightly","doing":true,"desc":"- Re-verified 2026-08-24 and REWORDED: the old claim \"re-reads every .md\" is stale — document bodies live in the in-memory set now, nothing touches the disk. What survives is the spirit: every `list_documents` call still runs a full UTF-8 encode of EVERY document's body just to report its size in bytes (query.ts:1055 `bytesOf(entry.body)`) — a number the original decode already knew and threw away. The call also allocates a filtered copy of the whole document list and a fresh broken-files map each time (query.ts:1039-1042).\n- The fix is unchanged in shape: remember the byte count on the Document record when the file is decoded; the listing then computes nothing per call.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T20:51:10-04:00","custom":{"agent":"grok","brief":"briefs/pldb.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24 20:35 (overnight, night 1 lane A)","merge":"AUTO (converged plan + the human's overnight word): pi review folded + CI green; gate = listing-sizes ≡ recompute differential + 5k bench artifact","pointers-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: substance unchanged, pointers drifted ~500 lines — bytesOf encodes the whole body at documents.ts:426, paid per document at query.ts:1055; the named fix lives at documents.ts:417-424","pr":"#375","worktree":".worktrees/list-documents-bytes"}}
{"id":"perf-filter-scope","parent":"psw2-server","ord":"a5","title":"file:/under: narrowing doesn't actually narrow the walk #nightly","doing":true,"desc":"- Scoping is a predicate applied inside the full walk, so a query scoped to one outline still visits every node in the vault; under: also calls ancestorsOf per node (filter.ts:1841-1855).\n- Rides behind search-index: an index that serves the grammar should serve the scopes too. byFile already covers the file: half.","after":["search-index"],"created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T21:33:51-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","brief":"briefs/fsc.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24 21:36 (overnight queue #1 trigger met: #374 merged + Opus slot freed)","merge":"AUTO iff the differential harness is green (converged gate); ANY divergence PARKS the lane","pointers-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: substance unchanged, pointer moved ~470 lines — inScopeOf iterates derived.nodes testing per node at filter.ts:2192-2199; scoping calls ancestorsOf per node for under: at :2316-2334","worktree":".worktrees/filter-scope"}}
{"id":"vaults-installed-deferrals","parent":"perfc-server","ord":"a2","title":"What PR #263 left, in so many words — the fold's reconnect cold-start, the missing composition bench, chat's fold adoption, one unpinned patch claim #deferral","done":"2026-08-19T19:39:56-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 from #263's deferrals section (the dag gate: a deferral becomes a roadmap node before the merge).\n\n- **(1)** a reconnect re-initialises the fold with freshly decoded entries while the store value-diffs and keeps identity — so after a link flap the per-record WeakMap search fold goes cold corpus-wide; design-ruled, worth its own look.\n- **(2)** no browser-side benchmark measures the composition a tab actually pays any more (kolu benches the merge, patch.bench the patch) — outlines.ts carries this note in its own text.\n- **(3)** `chat/state.ts`'s rows re-reads `seq` off every key and re-sorts the transcript per frame; transcript declares deltas so it gained fold too — an adoption opportunity the design never ruled on.\n- **(4)** `patch.test.ts` has no case for an upsert carrying no records — the file-arrives-empty-fills-empties-goes life was pinned only by the deleted `deriving.test.ts`; one format-suite case closes it.\n- (Deferral 6 of the PR — patch's flat-list allocation — is already filed as perf-patch-residue; 3 and 7 were deliberate and reasoned.)","created":"2026-08-19T18:11:31-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:43-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #263 deferrals","pr":"#265 merged 1cc4cd65"}}
{"id":"reconnect-seed-upstream","parent":"perfc-server","ord":"a1","title":"The reconnect seed's real home is upstream — kolu's syntheticSnapshot on the wire-snapshot path deletes olai's stopgap #deferral","done":"2026-08-20T10:28:07-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 at #265's merge (the dag gate: a deferral becomes a roadmap node before the merge).\n- olai #265 fixed the post-flap fold cold-start by seeding from the store (seedOf) and calls itself a stopgap in so many words.\n- kolu already has syntheticSnapshot and already uses it to seed a mid-stream registration; one line upstream on the wire-snapshot path makes init hand back the store's own objects.\n- When that lands: olai deletes seedOf, its test, and the bench's wire arm.\n- Author's bench for scale: one post-flap search 29.9ms wire-seeded vs 16.3ms store-held (980 files / 21,552 records).\n- **DONE 2026-08-20.** The olai half went first, for another reason: #279 (the flip) deleted seedOf, its test and the bench arm with the rest of the browser-held vault. The kolu half is kolu#2189 (merged 2d72179a5, Opus; grok do-not-object with an out-of-tree mutation check): the wire-snapshot arm seeds every fold from `syntheticSnapshot()` after `applySnapshot`, so a fold gets the store's own objects whether it registered before or after the snapshot — one answer, pinned by a reconnect-identity test. Downstream checked: drishti and odu register no folds; no pair PR.","created":"2026-08-19T19:39:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:43-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #265 deferral 1","repo":"kolu"}}
{"id":"vault-in-browser","parent":"perfc-server","ord":"a0","title":"The browser holds the whole vault — stops scaling at thousands of documents","done":"2026-08-20T07:26:38-04:00","desc":"The human's ruling, 2026-08-19, in their words: this is not a 'good' thing — when we have 1000s of .md files it will start to suck. To resolve.\n\n- **The target, ruled**: the browser can at most only have the CURRENT PAGE's data in memory — never the whole vault.\n- **Design**: brainstorming/vault-in-browser.md (Fable, 2026-08-19; iterated with the human in the designer's terminal). The wire goes page-scoped; the format layer does not move; the browser's half of the fold dies.\n- **Staging law, the human's words**: \"I won't accept 'The ugly coexistence'. Every PR must be self-contained, leaving no legacy code.\"\n- **The settled sequence — ten PRs**: (1) search-server-side [first; already its own node] · (2) tag vocabulary · (3) transcript id-marking · (4) calendar dots + agenda count · (5) pins · (6) fold re-filing · (7) read_node gains blocked-status · (8) the date index · (9) the offline overlay — 2–9 in any order, each complete on its own merits with its local walk deleted in the same diff · (10) LAST: the big one — the new wire member, all seven routes flipping to it, the whole-set machinery deleted, one diff, with the parity test and the before/after byte measurement riding it. PR 10 cannot be split: the law forbids both shipping the member unused and flipping routes one at a time; PRs 1–9 exist to shrink it.\n- **Both UX decisions RULED** (doc §5): (a) navigation may round-trip, cache nothing; (b) a dead wire freezes the app under an offline overlay.\n- #204 deflated one part; this replaces the model itself. Lanes dispatch on the human's word.","created":"2026-08-19T19:56:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:43-04:00","custom":{"done-story":"ALL TEN merged in one night (2026-08-19→20): #270 search, #271 transcript ids, #272 tags, #273 calendar, #274 pins, #275 blocked-status, #276 refile, #277 the offline overlay, #278 the date index, #279 THE FLIP (7e208f77) — the browser holds only the current page's data; first frame 1,679→135 kB (12×); the whole-set fold, DerivedProvider and seedOf are gone; parity property-tested per route before the old path died","from":"the human's ruling 2026-08-19","overnight":"APPROVED by the human 2026-08-19 via question tool: after the e2e cleanup merges, all TEN PRs run overnight on Opus, 3 lanes at a time (PR 1 first alone since 2–9 wait on it; PR 10 last, gated on 2–9) — every one auto-merges on its own green pipeline, none held for morning; deferrals fold into the same PR unless a strong reason is argued"}}
{"id":"search-server-side","parent":"perfc-search","ord":"a1","title":"Search goes entirely server-side — the first step out of vault-in-browser","done":"2026-08-20T00:52:43-04:00","desc":"Ruled by the human 2026-08-19: the browser's search boxes (⌘K palette, header box, filter bar) stop scanning the local copy and query the server instead.\n- Engineering that comes with it: per-keystroke round-trips need debounce + stale-response cancellation; results arrive async where they were sync; offline/flap behavior changes and must be decided, not inherited.\n- What it unlocks: the search index no longer needs to run in the browser — server-only shapes (bun:sqlite FTS5 trigram) become first-class candidates instead of a compromise. brainstorming/search-index.md rewrites on this premise.\n- The one-matcher rule bends, not breaks: whatever engine answers, ranking and the grammar stay defined in one place, and an oracle test pins server answers to the reference matcher.","see":["vault-in-browser"],"created":"2026-08-19T19:56:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:43-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human's ruling 2026-08-19","pr":"#270 merged 1954f3c3"}}
